## Running the job

Run the script docker_build_credinfoinitjob.sh to create the docker image. Push image to docker hub.
Copy sh and yml files to k8s host.
Update the settings in credinfoinitjob-dryrun.yml. In particular the JOB_PARMS settings will need to updated
to have the correct Vault url and token.

To make a dry-run of the job use credinfoinitjob-dryrun.sh, e.g.
   kubectl delete -f credinfoinitjob-dryrun.yml
   ./credinfoinitjob-dryrun.sh
   kubectl logs job/systems-credinfoinitjob-dryrun > ./credinfo_job.log

Check the logs to make sure all went all.

If you need to re-run the job delete the current job first using kubectl delete -f credinfoinitjob-dryrun.yml

To run and apply changes update credinfoinitjob-apply.yml and use credinfoinitjob-apply.sh
